{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/999883-2e-how-much-can-i-lift-bro","id":999883,"title":"[2E] How Much Can I Lift, Bro?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-11-07T12:35:12-08:00","id":999883,"title":"[2E] How Much Can I Lift, Bro?","content":"So I keep looking for any concrete rules for how much my characters can lift at a given amount of Strength. In first edition this was pretty clearly defined, but I can't find any similar rules in my second edition books. The closest thing I get is a 'Lifting Objects' action for the rules of Attributes under Strength, and it's a Strength + Stamina extended roll. However, it does not go on to explain what the target number of successes should be, how much I can lift at a given stat level, or anything like that.<br /> <br /> Am I missing something, or is that just not there? What can I do about this? I have players asking about it and it's really stumping us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:42:25-08:00","id":999891,"title":"","content":"I think it's just not there in 2E, probably because they decided that granular &quot;you can lift 1750 pounds&quot; measurements don't suit a more narrative system, which I would agree with. That being said, it would be good to have some kind of ballpark for what you simply can't do. Maybe &quot;if its Size is larger than your Strength+Stamina, you can't roll to lift/carry/throw it.&quot;<br /> <br /> If you wanted to do an extended roll, I think the general guidelines in the rules chapters for target number are enough to just eyeball it and pick a number.<br /> <br /> &quot;Five reflects a reasonable action that competent characters can achieve with the right tools and knowledge. Ten represents a difficult action that\u2019s still realistic<br /> for a professional in a field. Twenty represents a very difficult action that even a particularly skilled character will have trouble pulling off.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>2E Legacy Updates</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/978498-2e-legacy-update-brotherhood-of-the-demon-wind\" target=\"_blank\">Brotherhood of the Demon Wind</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/979249-2e-legacy-update-choir-of-hashmallim-with-bonus-content-about-summoning\" target=\"_blank\">Choir of Hashmallim</a> (plus extra Summoning content)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/980550-2e-legacy-update-storm-keepers\" target=\"_blank\">Storm Keepers</a>","edited":{"userid":2207,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","user":"Caladriu","date":". 11-07-2016, 03:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2207-caladriu","name":"Caladriu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1048"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T12:56:48-08:00","id":999905,"title":"","content":"You didn't miss anything. The 1e system was cut, and nothing replaced it. Since Hurt Locker will have Merits that allow lifting really heavy things, I'm hoping some rules will appear there.<br /> <br /> It's not the only omission, either. How do you tell how fast a normal human can climb a wall? AFAIK the only clue is the Parkour Style, which says how fast you can climb if you have it - you can extrapolate a speed for those who don't from that. But why should you have to extrapolate?<br /> <br /> There's the curious loss of the difference between a vertical jump and a broad jump in the &quot;Jumping&quot; action, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T13:12:35-08:00","id":999914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/999883-2e-how-much-can-i-lift-bro?p=999905#post999905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not the only omission, either. How do you tell how fast a normal human can climb a wall? AFAIK the only clue is the Parkour Style, which says how fast you can climb if you have it - you can extrapolate a speed for those who don't from that. But why should you have to extrapolate?</div> </div> </div> </div>Extrapolation is hardly needed. 'Without rolling, your character scales 10 feet + five feet per dot of Athletics as an instant action, <i>rather than the normal 10 feet</i>.'<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/999883-2e-how-much-can-i-lift-bro#post999883\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What can I do about this? I have players asking about it and it's really stumping us.</div> </div> </div> </div>You could use the first edition World of Darkness book, as Strength hasn't changed much, nor objects. What I'd do is just have your extended Strength + Resolve, or Athletics, depending on which is higher, with a penalty based on target's size. Add further modifiers as usual, is it squirming around? -2 Does your character have a lot of practice doing this? +2. Each roll of success is a turn of lifting it. One shouldn't have to roll for objects one can obviously carry, for instance size 3 or less that aren't strangely difficult to lift.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-07-2016, 04:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T14:34:33-08:00","id":999953,"title":"","content":"For me it usually works pretty well with the rough definitions of what each Attribute level should be.<br /> <br /> 1 is a weak, or even sick, person. I ask this gal to roll for any feat of strength bigger than lifting a book or carrying her own common stuff.<br /> <br /> 2 is a common person. If something seems out-of-ordinary, I ask for a roll, but most stuff don't need even that.<br /> <br /> 3 is a strong person. I will ask for a roll only for something I can clearly point out and call a &quot;feat of strength&quot;, if for a moderate person. I model it after strong people that aren't professional athletes yet.<br /> <br /> 4 is a heavy lifter athlete. Accordingly, I'll ask for rolls only for somewhat amazing feats. Things barely on the realm of human possibility. If it is <u>too clearly</u> in the realm of possibility, such a person shouldn't have to roll.<br /> <br /> 5 is the mortal peak. This is clearly one of the strongest people on Earth, there are moments on history, if brief, where no living mortal is at such level. Only the seemingly impossible should as much as require a roll from this person.<br /> <br /> I see no reason to call for a roll when its not dramatic, and it means I hardly see any reason to be so precise about lifting weight. Just going with those statements as guideline has been serving me pretty well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T17:59:25-08:00","id":1000056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/999883-2e-how-much-can-i-lift-bro?p=999953#post999953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see no reason to call for a roll when its not dramatic, and it means I hardly see any reason to be so precise about lifting weight.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much the long and short of it for me. I only ask for a roll when success and failure are both reasonable possibilities, and failure has dramatic consequences. Usually it's pretty easy to estimate if an object is within the realm of possibility for a person of below average/average/above average/exceptional/superlative strength to lift, and it's rare that not managing to lift a thing has significant enough consequences to merit a roll. On occasions where it does, I just use the basic extended action difficulty guidelines.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T18:10:43-08:00","id":1000062,"title":"","content":"Damn it, people, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/835933-lifting-charts-excised-deliberately?p=836310#post836310\">am I the only one who keeps these things stored in active memory?</a><br /> <br /> I mean, I agree about rolling only when dramatic, but the rules are <i>there</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T19:54:52-08:00","id":1000098,"title":"","content":"First, a Merit that changes the basic rules is not the natural place to look for how an ordinary use of a Skill works - the list of common actions, or (heaven help us) the Skill's description are where I would expect to find that information.<br /> <br /> Second, <i>Hurt Locker</i> has yet to be published - so unless you know to come here and dig through the Open Development drafts for material from that supplement, you won't find the rules for lifting stuff.<br /> <br /> Third, amechra, you posted that chart in February. Do you recall <i>everything</i> that was posted on this forum nine months ago?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1133-michael-brazier","name":"Michael Brazier","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"161"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-11-07T20:07:28-08:00","id":1000102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael Brazier</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/999883-2e-how-much-can-i-lift-bro?p=1000098#post1000098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Third, amechra, you posted that chart in February. Do you recall <i>everything</i> that was posted on this forum nine months ago?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />.<br /> <br /> (Not really - I was mostly acting aggravated for dramatic effect. I didn't actually expect anyone to remember.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}